 * `path: /screed-isolation` (child of the `acoustic` hub — already listed in
 * that hub's `children`). To avoid a duplicate-route build error the matching
 * branch is filtered out of getStaticPaths in src/pages/[...slug].astro — the
 * same pattern already used for acoustic-underlay, sports-track-underlay,
 * zainfit, zainsquare, zainduo, zainactive-rolls and curb-stone. The YAML entry
 * stays as data (still referenced by the acoustic hub nav / children list); this
 * file serves the URL.
 *
 * ─── DECISIONS TAKEN / FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 "Data Integrity" + §6) ─────────
 *  - PARENT HUB: the build request's JSON-LD names the breadcrumb parent
 *    "Acoustics & Construction Systems" at /acoustics-construction-systems.
 *    That route does not exist in this project — the real acoustic hub is
 *    /acoustic-soundproofing-flooring (screed-isolation.yaml `hub: acoustic`,
 *    and the hub already lists this page under `children`). Both the visible
 *    breadcrumb and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD below use the real path with the
 *    label "Acoustic & Soundproofing Flooring" — the same substitution already
 *    made on the acoustic-underlay and sports-track-underlay siblings.
 *    TODO: confirm the intended hub label / slug with the client.
 *  - CANONICAL HOST: the request shows "rukanalzain.com"; the configured site
 *    is "ruknalzain.ae" (astro.config.mjs). Canonical + all schema URLs are
 *    built from the configured site via BaseLayout `canonical={PATH}` (same
 *    choice as the siblings). TODO: confirm the production domain.
 *  - DESIGN SYSTEM: the request describes React / Lucide-React / a generic
 *    Tailwind palette. This is a static Astro site (zero-JS). The page follows
 *    the live charcoal / industrial-grey design system with a single amber
 *    action accent and bordered "ghost" WhatsApp buttons; Lucide icons are
 *    inlined as raw SVG path data (no runtime). FAQ accordion uses native
 *    <details>/<summary>.
 *  - H1 / METADATA: the request's H1 ("ZainSilence — High-Load Screed Isolation
 *    Systems Dubai") and title/description supersede the older copy in
 *    screed-isolation.yaml ("Zain Silence — High-Load Screed Isolation System"),
 *    the same way the sibling pages diverged from their YAML records. The YAML
 *    stays as-is for the hub nav.
 *  - TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS: screed-isolation.yaml lists thickness options,
 *    load capacity (kN/m²) and density (kg/m³) as null "to collect". Every spec
 *    row rendered below is the descriptive text supplied in the page-build
 *    request, NOT numeric data from Rukn_Al_Zain_SEO_Content_Brief.docx. Treat
 *    as PROVISIONAL and confirm against real product test data / manufacturer
 *    certificates before go-live.
 *  - STRUCTURED DATA: a single combined @graph (BreadcrumbList + Product +
 *    FAQPage) is emitted inline. The request supplied BreadcrumbList + FAQPage;
 *    the Product node is added per CLAUDE.md §5. Organization JSON-LD is emitted
 *    sitewide by BaseLayout.
 *
 * ─── IMAGE ASSETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * public/images/screed-isolation/ — all 1376×768, intrinsic dimensions wired
 * below to prevent layout shift:
 *   - zainsilence-hero-product.jpg
